01:58:34,800 --> 01:58:36,480
when the teacher's not there most of the time.

390
01:58:36,480 --> 01:58:39,280
We take a very smart,

391
01:58:39,280 --> 01:58:43,120
smart, hardworking, informed person to keep going when the teacher doesn't go.

392
01:58:43,120 --> 01:58:45,440
So, maybe that's the story. All right.

393
01:58:45,440 --> 01:58:47,760
So, that and then finally,

394
01:58:47,760 --> 01:58:52,080
there is a literature usually called the employer learning literature.

395
01:58:52,080 --> 01:58:54,280
Where they go and try to basically,

396
01:58:54,280 --> 01:58:56,400
or it's not learning, it's learning.

397
01:58:56,400 --> 01:59:02,800
Learning literature. This is where the researchers go and get some measure of your true ability,

398
01:59:02,800 --> 01:59:06,040
like IQ, they assume it's not accessible to employers.

399
01:59:06,040 --> 01:59:09,240
And then they see, well,

400
01:59:09,240 --> 01:59:13,720
how does the return to ability, to your true ability,

401
01:59:13,720 --> 01:59:15,920
compare to the return to education over time?

402
01:59:15,920 --> 01:59:19,080
And normally, what they find is that the longer you work,

403
01:59:19,080 --> 01:59:22,760
the lower the return to education and the higher the return to ability.

404
01:59:22,760 --> 01:59:24,600
And they normally interpret this as learning.

405
01:59:24,600 --> 01:59:26,000
So, basically, this means, suppose that you're

406
01:59:26,000 --> 01:59:27,920
a really smart person who drops out of high school.

