So, there is a sub-literature on the effect of education on IQ.

38
01:61:49,640 --> 01:61:53,160
So, again, there's zero doubt that IQ causes education.

39
01:61:53,160 --> 01:61:56,800
So, you can get someone's IQ goes from under seven,

40
01:61:56,800 --> 01:61:59,760
and use that to predict their ultimate educational attainment.

41
01:61:59,760 --> 01:62:02,560
Of course, this is a point where everyone's,

42
01:62:02,560 --> 01:62:05,320
at seven, everyone has the same number of years of education virtually,

43
01:62:05,320 --> 01:62:08,560
except for a few kids that went out back or something like that.

44
01:62:08,560 --> 01:62:11,280
So, anyway, so IQ definitely causes education.

45
01:62:11,280 --> 01:62:15,080
There is a separate literature on the extent to which education causes IQ,

46
01:62:15,080 --> 01:62:17,920
and a lot of evidence that it does,

47
01:62:17,920 --> 01:62:20,760
and including a lot of quasi-experimental evidence

48
01:62:20,760 --> 01:62:24,360
that if you just send a person an extra year of school,

49
01:62:24,360 --> 01:62:25,600
their IQ will be higher.

50
01:62:25,600 --> 01:62:29,240
There's only, there's just two main problems with this result.

51
01:62:29,240 --> 01:62:33,400
I wish we're getting a generally acknowledged among people that are paying attention.

52
01:62:33,400 --> 01:62:35,200
We get to see who's paying attention.

53
01:62:35,200 --> 01:62:37,160
Psychologists are only paying attention.

54
01:62:37,160 --> 01:62:39,880
Economists are likely to just quickly read the abstract and say,

55
01:62:39,880 --> 01:62:42,520
see, education raises intelligence.

56
01:62:42,520 --> 01:62:46,080
But I get my psychologist's work on this will tell you is two problems.

57
01:62:46,080 --> 01:62:47,560
One of them is fade out.

58
01:62:47,560 --> 01:62:51,080
So that while a year of education noticeably raises your IQ,

59
01:62:51,080 --> 01:62:53,400
a lot of the gain goes away over time.

60
01:62:53,400 --> 01:62:56,200
And this is true for almost anything that raises IQ.

61
01:62:56,200 --> 01:62:59,640
Like any intervention that raises IQ is likely not to last.

62
01:62:59,640 --> 01:63:01,760
So, like you just go back to where you would have been.

63
01:63:01,760 --> 01:63:03,120
So, this is the fade out problem.

64
01:63:03,120 --> 01:63:07,800
And the other problem is what's called the problem of hollow gains.

65
01:63:09,280 --> 01:63:12,320
What do you think of as teaching the test?

66
01:63:12,320 --> 01:63:18,000
Right, so what is the easiest way to dramatically raise IQ?

67
01:63:18,000 --> 01:63:19,520
What's that?

68
01:63:19,520 --> 01:63:21,240
Practice IQ test.

69
01:63:21,240 --> 01:63:22,640
Even easier.

70
01:63:22,640 --> 01:63:24,760
This takes about one minute.

71
01:63:24,760 --> 01:63:28,560
This is a one minute path to getting super genius IQ.

72
01:63:28,560 --> 01:63:30,360
Works for sure.

73
01:63:30,360 --> 01:63:31,360
Answer key.

74
01:63:31,360 --> 01:63:35,520
Just give the person the answer key and that will raise their IQ score up to like 200,

75
01:63:35,520 --> 01:63:37,240
250 really easily.

76
01:63:37,240 --> 01:63:38,640
Works like a charm.

77
01:63:38,640 --> 01:63:39,240
All right.

78
01:63:39,240 --> 01:63:44,440
But I don't know anyone so naive as to say let's just give everybody an IQ test and

79
01:63:44,440 --> 01:63:46,720
our country will all be geniuses.

80
01:63:46,720 --> 01:63:49,000
Right, nobody thinks that because we realize well,

81
01:63:49,000 --> 01:63:51,640
that's not raising IQ in the right way.

82
01:63:51,640 --> 01:63:53,920
All right, now once you realize that,

83
01:63:53,920 --> 01:63:57,600
that at least some increases in IQ are not really meaningful,

84
01:63:57,600 --> 01:64:01,120
even though they're large, then you have to start thinking, well, what about other things?

85
01:64:01,120 --> 01:64:05,040
So what about practicing IQ tests?

86
01:64:05,040 --> 01:64:05,920
What about doing that?

87
01:64:05,920 --> 01:64:11,080
Well, there is a lot of evidence that if you just send someone to a prep class,

88
01:64:11,080 --> 01:64:13,160
that will boost their scores.

89
01:64:13,160 --> 01:64:18,720
Right, and you can just practice or do a lot of practice and then your IQ score goes up.

90
01:64:18,720 --> 01:64:24,120
But how many people think that SAT prep classes actually make you truly smarter?

91
01:64:24,120 --> 01:64:24,600
Very few.

92
01:64:24,600 --> 01:64:28,440
And one thing that intelligence research will tell you is that if you practice for

93
01:64:28,440 --> 01:64:30,600
one particular kind of IQ test, but

94
01:64:30,600 --> 01:64:35,880
then take a totally different kind of IQ test, you will not have improved at all.

95
01:64:35,880 --> 01:64:38,240
You either lose one symptom of the hollowness of the gains.

96
01:64:38,240 --> 01:64:42,480
All right, then you might start thinking, well, what about education?

97
01:64:42,480 --> 01:64:44,000
Is that hollow?

98
01:64:44,000 --> 01:64:49,160
Well, for a lot of tests at least, it's very hollow because very often,

99
01:64:49,160 --> 01:64:53,800
the very things that are IQ tests are specifically taught to you in class.

100
01:64:53,800 --> 01:64:57,200
So like there is a standard IQ test that asks you to go and

101
01:64:57,200 --> 01:64:58,680
name the biggest river in Africa.

102
01:64:58,680 --> 01:65:01,520
And you're like, that's an IQ test?

103
01:65:01,520 --> 01:65:03,840
That's not an IQ test, yes.

104
01:65:03,840 --> 01:65:07,760
And psychometrically, this does correlate very well with other items.

105
01:65:07,760 --> 01:65:10,840
So it's fine as long as you're not trying to game the system.

106
01:65:10,840 --> 01:65:15,520
But once you start trying to game the system, then not so useful anymore.

107
01:65:15,520 --> 01:65:19,680
All right, and there's a general literature on test prep as a way of

108
01:65:19,680 --> 01:65:21,000
improving people's performance, and

109
01:65:21,000 --> 01:65:25,040
test prep is super effective compared to really learning stuff.

110
01:65:26,320 --> 01:65:29,360
So you can either go and teach people, teach them the test, or

111
01:65:29,360 --> 01:65:31,160
you can improve their general knowledge.

112
01:65:31,160 --> 01:65:35,040
Right, so anyway, so teaching the test is very effective, but

113
01:65:35,040 --> 01:65:37,640
it doesn't inspire a lot of confidence, does it?

114
01:65:37,640 --> 01:65:39,160
If you just hear, yeah, well, their scores are up,

115
01:65:39,160 --> 01:65:40,920
then you just talk to the test.

116
01:65:40,920 --> 01:65:44,960
So, scores is score, right?

117
01:65:44,960 --> 01:65:45,480
Yes?

118
01:65:45,480 --> 01:65:47,360
With regards to the river in Africa question,

119
01:65:47,360 --> 01:65:50,600
is the biggest river in Africa also the only river in Africa that most

120
01:65:50,600 --> 01:65:53,520
Westerners probably know, or is it just the Nile?

121
01:65:53,520 --> 01:65:55,280
So a lot of people get the question wrong.

122
01:65:55,280 --> 01:66:00,560
So Kim, it's one where basically smart people tend to know the answer and

123
01:66:00,560 --> 01:66:02,480
not so smart people don't tend to know the answer.

124
01:66:04,520 --> 01:66:07,160
Okay, and that's all the, in terms of designing an IQ test,

125
01:66:07,160 --> 01:66:11,160
all you need is that the items correlate with the thing that you are really

126
01:66:11,160 --> 01:66:14,560
trying to measure, but in terms of gaming the system, on the other hand,

127
01:66:14,560 --> 01:66:16,480
not so good, right?

128
01:66:16,480 --> 01:66:20,280
And anyway, so now, of course, there are IQ tests that go out of the way to be

129
01:66:20,280 --> 01:66:22,120
what are called cultural reduced,

130
01:66:22,120 --> 01:66:24,800
where you don't have things that you think are taught in a classroom.

131
01:66:24,800 --> 01:66:27,160
But even there, these are things like geometric puzzles.

132
01:66:27,160 --> 01:66:29,680
Do you ever have geometric puzzles in a classroom?

133
01:66:29,680 --> 01:66:34,480
Yeah, so even there, it's like, well, geometry is a culture or not culture?

134
01:66:34,480 --> 01:66:38,080
And can you train people to do well in a geometry test?

135
01:66:38,080 --> 01:66:42,280
You sure can, so you're not self-convincing.

136
01:66:42,280 --> 01:66:45,120
To me, my favorite IQ test is just lunch.

137
01:66:45,120 --> 01:66:46,000
It's just talk at lunch.

138
01:66:46,000 --> 01:66:47,720
Now I will decide what you're eating.

139
01:66:47,720 --> 01:66:51,960
And that can't be gamed.

140
01:66:51,960 --> 01:66:53,520
But this is a controversial view.

141
01:66:53,520 --> 01:66:56,560
It's not generally accepted by psychologists.

142
01:66:56,560 --> 01:66:57,080
Yes?

143
01:66:57,080 --> 01:67:00,040
So you really can't have a non-hollow IQ test, can you?

144
01:67:00,040 --> 01:67:01,960
Because eventually, people can game these tests, right?

145
01:67:01,960 --> 01:67:05,240
Well, so it's not generally that people talk about a hollow test.

146
01:67:05,240 --> 01:67:07,800
They talk about hollow games.

147
01:67:07,800 --> 01:67:09,040
It's the games that are hollow.

148
01:67:09,040 --> 01:67:12,080
So basically, you give the test.

149
01:67:12,080 --> 01:67:14,360
When you first design the test, no one's practiced it.

150
01:67:14,360 --> 01:67:18,520
And then you can say, well, this is a fair measure of what we're really going at.

151
01:67:18,520 --> 01:67:21,320
But then once there's room to game it, then-

152
01:67:21,320 --> 01:67:22,680
You have to keep redesigning it.

153
01:67:22,680 --> 01:67:26,200
Yeah, so yeah, you're sort of always trying to keep one step ahead of people

154
01:67:26,200 --> 01:67:27,280
in gaming it.

155
01:67:27,280 --> 01:67:29,200
On the General Sub-Survey, they actually

156
01:67:29,200 --> 01:67:31,560
have a short 10-word IQ test.

157
01:67:31,560 --> 01:67:32,680
So it's a vocabulary test.

158
01:67:32,680 --> 01:67:37,160
But again, it correlates quite well with normal IQ tests.

159
01:67:37,160 --> 01:67:40,200
But they keep the words secret.

160
01:67:40,200 --> 01:67:42,400
The words on that test are secret.

161
01:67:42,400 --> 01:67:43,920
They don't share them.

162
01:67:43,920 --> 01:67:45,640
Because they're worried that if they announce them,

163
01:67:45,640 --> 01:67:48,200
that they might actually raise public knowledge of the words

164
01:67:48,200 --> 01:67:51,520
and then invalidate their own test.

165
01:67:51,520 --> 01:67:54,440
All right, so anyway, so the book has a lot of other evidence.

166
01:67:54,440 --> 01:67:58,280
But my general story is that the evidence for signaling

167
01:67:58,280 --> 01:68:01,560
is so overwhelming, you have to be really delusional not to admit

168
01:68:01,560 --> 01:68:03,160
that it's a huge force in the world.

169
01:68:03,160 --> 01:68:07,560
And yet, I do show that there are many prominent labor and education

170
01:68:07,560 --> 01:68:09,640
economists who are totally dismissive of it.

171
01:68:09,640 --> 01:68:14,280
And they're dismissive just by not talking about it.

172
01:68:14,280 --> 01:68:16,520
And that is very prevalent.

173
01:68:16,520 --> 01:68:19,640
So if you just go to Google Scholar and you Google, say,

174
01:68:19,640 --> 01:68:22,920
human capital, in quotes, versus educational signaling, in quotes,

175
01:68:22,920 --> 01:68:26,080
I think there's like 1,000 to 1 imbalance.

176
01:68:26,080 --> 01:68:28,120
So anyway, it's an enormous imbalance.

177
01:68:28,120 --> 01:68:31,960
So there's a lot of ignoring it by omission and just saying it.

178
01:68:31,960 --> 01:68:35,440
And of course, if you spend 99% of your time on one theory

179
01:68:35,440 --> 01:68:38,480
compared to another one, which theory are you basically saying

180
01:68:38,480 --> 01:68:40,440
is the one thing that's true?

181
01:68:40,440 --> 01:68:42,640
The one you spend almost all your time on, especially

182
01:68:42,640 --> 01:68:45,160
if you're a empirical person.

183
01:68:45,160 --> 01:68:47,880
Anyway, then on top of that, I do find all the people

184
01:68:47,880 --> 01:68:51,200
that have rendered their general verdicts on how important signaling is.

185
01:68:51,200 --> 01:68:54,920
And out of the empirical economists who have talked about it generally,

186
01:68:54,920 --> 01:68:56,240
it's very dismissive.

187
01:68:56,240 --> 01:68:59,360
So I move along, nothing to see here.

188
01:68:59,360 --> 01:69:04,760
And in terms of the arguments, so in the book I talk about,

189
01:69:04,760 --> 01:69:07,000
what they're saying, a lot of it just comes down

190
01:69:07,000 --> 01:69:12,400
to attacking a really simplistic version of the model.

191
01:69:12,400 --> 01:69:15,160
One that I've heard many times is, look, if education was signaling,

192
01:69:15,160 --> 01:69:16,400
we'd just do IQ tests instead.

193
01:69:16,400 --> 01:69:17,080
So it can't be.

194
01:69:17,080 --> 01:69:19,240
The end.

195
01:69:19,240 --> 01:69:21,280
Well, that's a very good argument against the view

196
01:69:21,280 --> 01:69:24,400
that education is purely a signal of intelligence.

197
01:69:24,400 --> 01:69:27,040
It's not a very good answer to the view that education

198
01:69:27,040 --> 01:69:31,160
signals that package, especially when you realize

199
01:69:31,160 --> 01:69:35,560
that if someone were to come up with a radical, unconventional, new,

200
01:69:35,560 --> 01:69:39,040
original, alternative way of signaling conformity,

201
01:69:39,040 --> 01:69:40,520
what would that actually signal?

202
01:69:40,520 --> 01:69:43,080
Who's going to be the first in line to do the radical, new way

203
01:69:43,080 --> 01:69:44,960
of signaling the conformity?

204
01:69:44,960 --> 01:69:45,800
Nonconformists.

205
01:69:45,800 --> 01:69:50,440
There is a built-in catch-22 here, which I say tends to lock in the system.

206
01:69:50,440 --> 01:69:53,280
Another ridiculous thing I've heard economists say to my face

207
01:69:53,280 --> 01:69:57,080
is, look, the current system passes the market test.

208
01:69:57,080 --> 01:69:59,200
The current system receives about a trillion dollars

209
01:69:59,200 --> 01:70:01,720
in government subsidies a year.

210
01:70:01,720 --> 01:70:04,480
There is no industry that I know of that has not done less

211
01:70:04,480 --> 01:70:07,160
to pass the market test than this one.

212
01:70:07,160 --> 01:70:09,580
In fact, if you're getting a trillion dollars in subsidies,

213
01:70:09,580 --> 01:70:11,720
isn't that a sign that you would be destroyed

214
01:70:11,720 --> 01:70:14,160
if you had to pass the market test?

215
01:70:14,160 --> 01:70:16,080
Terrible argument.

216
01:70:16,080 --> 01:70:19,040
And then another one just says, look, there's got to be a cheaper way.

217
01:70:19,040 --> 01:70:20,560
There's got to be a cheaper way.

218
01:70:20,560 --> 01:70:23,840
And again, that's, look, trillion dollars in subsidies, first of all.

219
01:70:23,840 --> 01:70:27,200
So why would people be looking around for a cheaper way

220
01:70:27,200 --> 01:70:30,080
when the current way is so heavily subsidized?

221
01:70:30,080 --> 01:70:33,280
And then, of course, you can add on the conformity issue, which really,

222
01:70:33,280 --> 01:70:37,040
really undermines the incentives to look around for something else.

223
01:70:37,040 --> 01:70:39,920
And then on top of it, there's the point I was making about wedding rings.

224
01:70:39,920 --> 01:70:43,640
Look, if someone did come up with a much cheaper way of making a diamond

225
01:70:43,640 --> 01:70:48,080
ring, would the result be that we get to have cheap weddings from now on?

226
01:70:48,080 --> 01:70:52,720
No, the result would be that we'd have to find another expensive way

227
01:70:52,720 --> 01:70:54,240
of signaling devotion.

228
01:70:54,240 --> 01:70:57,760
Similarly, if someone came up with a way of making education really cheap,

229
01:70:57,760 --> 01:71:00,600
what would we wind up doing?

230
01:71:00,600 --> 01:71:03,280
Doing more education, more years.

231
01:71:03,280 --> 01:71:06,440
Because if it were cheap enough, everyone does it.

232
01:71:06,440 --> 01:71:09,080
If everyone does it, what does it signal?

233
01:71:09,080 --> 01:71:10,320
Nothing.

234
01:71:10,320 --> 01:71:13,400
And what do you have to do in order to signal when everyone else is signaling

235
01:71:13,400 --> 01:71:14,120
nothing?

236
01:71:14,120 --> 01:71:16,760
More than what they're doing.

237
01:71:16,760 --> 01:71:18,680
So that is my story.

238
01:71:21,720 --> 01:71:24,200
Just to be clear, what I'm telling you is not the normal view

239
01:71:24,200 --> 01:71:26,040
among computer specialists.

240
01:71:26,040 --> 01:71:27,080
Not at all.

241
01:71:27,080 --> 01:71:29,840
This is a case where I'm just saying the people specializing in this

242
01:71:29,840 --> 01:71:36,440
are so far wrong that they really don't know which way is up.

243
01:71:36,440 --> 01:71:39,920
Part of my complaint is that there's a lot of evidence outside of economics

244
01:71:39,920 --> 01:71:42,000
that's on point, and they don't have any interest in it,

245
01:71:42,000 --> 01:71:44,240
or refuse to read it, or aren't even aware of it.

246
01:71:44,240 --> 01:71:46,640
So you have evidence like educational psychology,

247
01:71:46,640 --> 01:71:49,080
industrial psychology, sociology.

248
01:71:49,080 --> 01:71:53,720
And then there's also a whole academic discipline called education.

249
01:71:53,720 --> 01:71:54,240
Called that.

250
01:71:54,240 --> 01:71:57,160
There's departments of education on campuses.

251
01:71:57,160 --> 01:72:01,040
And education economists generally don't pay any attention to their existence.

252
01:72:01,040 --> 01:72:04,120
But they're there, and they know things.

253
01:72:04,120 --> 01:72:07,880
So I say they should pay attention to those, to what they're saying.

254
01:72:07,880 --> 01:72:12,000
Anyway, so of course, it's just my opinion.

255
01:72:12,000 --> 01:72:13,200
All right.

256
01:72:13,200 --> 01:72:13,720
Let's see.

257
01:72:13,720 --> 01:72:15,240
Questions about education signaling?

258
01:72:15,240 --> 01:72:15,720
Thank you.

259
01:72:15,720 --> 01:72:17,200
Yeah.

260
01:72:17,200 --> 01:72:17,680
Happy?

261
01:72:17,680 --> 01:72:18,680
So.

262
01:72:18,680 --> 01:72:20,640
All right.

263
01:72:20,640 --> 01:72:21,160
All right.

264
01:72:21,160 --> 01:72:22,720
And then some other ones.

265
01:72:22,720 --> 01:72:24,840
So here's one that Robin Hanks has put forward.

266
01:72:24,840 --> 01:72:26,760
First, I thought it was crazy when I heard it.

267
01:72:26,760 --> 01:72:29,520
And increasingly, I think there's at least a lot to it.

268
01:72:29,520 --> 01:72:32,520
I don't think it's nearly as knocked down as educational signaling.

269
01:72:32,520 --> 01:72:35,080
But Robin says, you know, a lot of health care

270
01:72:35,080 --> 01:72:36,760
isn't really about improving your health.

271
01:72:36,760 --> 01:72:38,480
A lot of it is about signaling.

272
01:72:38,480 --> 01:72:39,000
All right.

273
01:72:39,000 --> 01:72:41,000
So just like, why would you think this?

274
01:72:41,000 --> 01:72:44,120
Well, Robin begins with this big empirical literature

275
01:72:44,120 --> 01:72:46,800
that tries to estimate the effect of medicine on health.

276
01:72:46,800 --> 01:72:50,880
And finds that at least marginal medicine seems to do very little good.

277
01:72:50,880 --> 01:72:54,840
So there are a number of experiments where they randomly assign people

278
01:72:54,840 --> 01:72:56,520
to different levels of insurance.

279
01:72:56,520 --> 01:73:00,360
And as you expect, people with better insurance get more health care.

280
01:73:00,360 --> 01:73:04,720
But then they don't seem to actually have better health on almost any measure.

281
01:73:04,720 --> 01:73:07,920
Furthermore, there's a lot of things where there are regional variations

282
01:73:07,920 --> 01:73:12,680
in either the cost of health care or access.

283
01:73:12,680 --> 01:73:15,160
Things like if you're just further away from a hospital.

284
01:73:15,160 --> 01:73:16,920
So a lot of empirical work where they try

285
01:73:16,920 --> 01:73:20,280
to use these quasi-experimental designs to see how much does it

286
01:73:20,280 --> 01:73:23,080
matter if you have better or worse access to health care.

287
01:73:23,080 --> 01:73:25,360
